{"op":"add","path":"/elements/methodology","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"This analysis used 12 months of MRR records broken down by plan tier. Net new MRR was computed each month as new customer MRR plus expansion MRR minus churned MRR. The month with the highest net new MRR was flagged as the peak. The waterfall shows how each component (new, expansion, churn) contributed to that month's total. Plan-level figures reflect all customers on each pricing tier during the peak month. Use the Plan filter to isolate a single tier's contribution across all months.","variant":"body"},"children":[]}}
